  "i18n": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Roll & Turn Maze",
      "concept": "Instead of walking through the maze, you turn the whole box 90°. Every turn, Koro the ball and the wooden crates all fall until they stop. Crates can cover spikes, become ledges, stop you, or block you. Reading which order of turns drops Koro into the hole is the core.",
      "howToPlay": "Swipe left/right (or the ⟲⟳ buttons) to turn the box 90°. Drop Koro into the ◎ hole. Hit a spike and you can undo one move.",
      "libraryDecision": "None. Motion is cell-by-cell falling; a physics engine would make stopping points fuzzy and break the reading puzzle. Plain Canvas rotates a 2D board smoothly enough.",
      "soundDecision": "No BGM, to keep thinking time quiet. A stone grinding sound when the box turns, a marble clack and a crate thud whose strength depends on fall distance, plus gem and goal chimes, convey weight and feedback by ear."
    }
  },
